.TITLE "kill"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Sends a signal to a process. It is primarily used to __terminate processes__ by sending the SIGTERM signal to a specified process ID.

.DIV "ALIAS"

.DIV "TLDR"
**kill pid**
Sends the default termination signal to a process.
> __pid__ the process identification number

**kill -l**
Lists all available signal names and numbers.
> __-l__ list signals flag

**kill -9 pid**
Forcefully terminates a process by sending the SIGKILL signal.
> __-9__ SIGKILL signal flag

**kill -s signal_name pid**
Sends a specific signal to a process by name.
> __-s__ signal flag | __signal_name__ the name of the signal

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Always try to use the default __kill__ (SIGTERM) first to allow a process to shut down gracefully. Use the __-9__ (SIGKILL) flag only as a last resort when a process is unresponsive and cannot be terminated otherwise.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:ps** **mac:top**

